  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency agricultural and livelihood support in Marib and Sa&apos;adah governorates</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide food security to vulnerable communities affected by conflict. This FAO project provides the assistance which is channelled through a cash+ approach, which includes the provision of in-kind agricultural inputs together with season-specific cash assistance to mitigate against the impact of food insecurity and malnutrition among the most vulnerable households. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 25,620 people, including 12,580 women, 13,040 men, and including 5,000 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
